This project is a C#/.NET port of the git-diff-view project, with an Avalonia
rendering layer.

Portions of the design, parsing logic, algorithms, and behavior are based on or
derived from:

git-diff-view
Copyright (c) 2022 MrWangJustToDo
Licensed under the MIT License
https://github.com/MrWangJustToDo/git-diff-view

The diff parser ported through git-diff-view (Services/DiffParser.cs) originates
from GitHub Desktop:

desktop
Copyright (c) GitHub, Inc.
Licensed under the MIT License
https://github.com/desktop/desktop

The HTML escaping utility ported through git-diff-view (Utils/EscapeHtml.cs)
originates from the Vue.js core packages/shared/src/escape-html.ts, licensed
under the MIT License.

The character-level diff implementation (Services/FastDiff.cs) is a C# port of:

fast-diff
Copyright (c) Jason Chen <jhchen7@gmail.com>
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
https://github.com/jhchen/fast-diff

fast-diff itself modifies the diff-match-patch library by Neil Fraser.

The golden-test harness (tests/js-harness) bundles the TypeScript sources of
git-diff-view and fast-diff@1.3.0 with esbuild to generate reference data at
development time. These sources are test-only inputs and are not distributed
with the compiled libraries or NuGet packages.

Syntax highlighting (M5) is built on:

TextMateSharp (grammar tokenization engine, with its Onigwrap oniguruma binding)
Copyright (c) 2022 danipascual
Licensed under the MIT License
https://github.com/danipascual/TextMateSharp

The scope-to-color theme matching (Services/TextMate/ScopeThemeMatcher.cs) is a
C# port of the vscode-textmate theme matcher as bundled with shiki:

vscode-textmate / @shikijs/vscode-textmate
Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation
Licensed under the MIT License

The embedded TextMate grammars (Resources/TextMate/grammars) and the GitHub
light/dark themes (Resources/TextMate/themes) are extracted from the shiki
bundled languages and themes:

shiki (@shikijs/langs, @shikijs/themes)
Copyright (c) 2021 Anthony Fu
Licensed under the MIT License

The individual grammar files originate from their upstream VS Code language
extensions and keep their respective licenses (MIT / TextMate license); the
github-light/github-dark themes originate from the GitHub Visual Studio Code
theme (MIT). Extraction happens at development time via
tests/js-harness/extract-textmate.mjs, which also normalizes capture
shorthand and converts/drops the begin/while rules TextMateSharp cannot
compile.
